@cpmpml as many pointed out above, this is a particularly hard rule to enforce. Team can always say "well, only 6 people actively contributes to this competition effort, the Twitter post was to promote the startup of 12, etc." and Kaggle can't prove anything.

With that being said, a natural assumption is that the 12 people in the tweet are developing some generalized tech, and only a handful of people (6 team members on Kaggle) actively uses the company's tech to contribute to this Kaggle competition.

With Kaggle having more and more high-visibility competitions (ARC-AGI, AIMO, etc.), we will see more of similar situations where companies participate with their tech, making the "team" boundary harder to prove or enforce. AIMO actually had a pretty lazy solution: just increase team size to 20.
